Feature: Reconcile only a fictional offline sample client with v2
  A-S136 / D-S136 / SC-S136 is one frozen satisfier unit.
  Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result
  Connectivity, identity, pending changes, receipts, effects and elapsed times are
  fixed fictional teaching data, not a device, network, authentication or storage operation.

  Background:
    Given sample-client-136, fictional-user-136 and two fixed queued changes
    And the operator console and two other fictional workers remain available
    And the protocol uses stable operation IDs, authenticated ownership, revision checks
    And an accepted v2 receipt and exactly one correct effect are required per change
    And the synthetic offline budget is 5000 ms and recovery budget is 200 ms

  Scenario: Disconnect only the sample, queue, reconnect and reconcile with v2
    When the operator takes only the sample client offline
    And inspects the operator console while the sample remains offline
    And queues the two fixed changes and reconnects the sample
    And synchronizes with the clean receipt fixture within both budgets
    Then both correct effects have count one and matching authenticated v2 receipts
    And no pending change remains and the measured result is positive
    And the console and other workers remain available throughout the retained history

  Scenario: A conflict is observed, never silently merged
    Given the sample reconnects with both changes pending
    When synchronization observes a revision conflict on the second change
    Then one effect is confirmed and the conflicting change remains pending
    And the result is negative with interrupted user impact
    And no merge, acknowledgment, successful retry or second effect is invented

  Scenario: A missing acknowledgment is unresolved until the same ID is confirmed
    Given the sample reconnects with both changes pending
    When synchronization observes both effects but no first-change acknowledgment
    Then the first change remains pending and the result is unknown
    When the operator retries that same pending ID against the fixed deduplication receipt
    Then the effect count remains one, its attempt count becomes two and pending clears
    And the positive result does not erase the earlier unknown observation

  Scenario Outline: Known incorrect or over-budget observations cannot pass
    Given the sample reconnects with both changes pending
    When synchronization uses <fixture> with <timing>
    Then the result is negative and reports the actual synthetic reason
    And confirmed receipts are not invented for any unresolved change
    Examples:
      | fixture          | timing               |
      | duplicate-effect | within-budget        |
      | identity-rejected| within-budget        |
      | clean            | offline-over-budget  |
      | clean            | recovery-over-budget |

  Scenario: Strict typed inputs and state ordering reject invalid actions atomically
    When an action is missing, malformed, includes extra data or uses an unknown fixture
    Or synchronization is attempted before offline queuing and reconnection
    Then a specific error is exposed without altering pending changes, effects or history
    And the operator controls still work
    And incomplete observation evidence cannot be presented as success

  Scenario: Keyboard, error and reset affordances remain usable
    When the operator conducts the lesson using Tab, Enter and Space
    And a malformed control value or premature action is rejected in the actual DOM
    And the operator resets the rehearsal
    Then active fixtures, counters and errors return to their initial values
    And previous results remain visible in a bounded in-memory journal
    And any omitted old journal entries are explicitly counted

  Scenario: Actual browser safety and failure observations
    Given a directly opened local lesson with external local scripts and styles
    Then CSP blocks inline script execution and connection attempts
    And no management, cloud, credentials, persistent storage or machine-offline API is used
    And an unavailable model produces an explicit startup error, not a successful result
    And the published isolated helper is closed in an awaited finally block
